WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Pause before moving on.

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:14.520
Let the previous task be exactly where it is: complete, incomplete, or waiting for someone else.

3
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.420
Feel the support beneath your body.

4
00:00:24.982 --> 00:00:26.862
Notice what your hands are doing.

5
00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:32.942
Set down anything you do not need for the next minute.

6
00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:41.862
Let the eyes look away from the last task and find one neutral shape or color.

7
00:00:48.424 --> 00:00:50.224
Take an ordinary breath in.

8
00:00:51.924 --> 00:01:02.639
As you breathe out, allow one small sign of ending: close a window, place a note, or simply say finished for now.

9
00:01:10.841 --> 00:01:15.236
The mind may keep rehearsing what just happened.

10
00:01:16.936 --> 00:01:21.091
You do not have to force it silent.

11
00:01:22.791 --> 00:01:33.776
Feel the next inhale while the thoughts continue, and feel the next exhale without following them further.

12
00:01:43.619 --> 00:01:46.579
Adjust your posture for what comes next.

13
00:01:48.279 --> 00:01:55.444
Perhaps sit back, stand, turn, or let the shoulders move.

14
00:01:57.144 --> 00:02:02.554
Choose comfort and alertness rather than a perfect pose.

15
00:02:09.116 --> 00:02:13.311
Name the next task in a few plain words.

16
00:02:15.011 --> 00:02:17.971
Then name only its first action.

17
00:02:19.671 --> 00:02:21.391
Keep it small enough to begin.

18
00:02:29.593 --> 00:02:34.168
Feel feet, seat, or hands once more.

19
00:02:35.868 --> 00:02:38.748
One task can end without being erased.

20
00:02:40.448 --> 00:02:45.103
Another can begin without carrying everything at once.

21
00:02:51.665 --> 00:02:53.265
Look toward the first action.

22
00:02:54.965 --> 00:03:00.000
When you are ready, move into it at an unhurried pace.
